{
  "_comment": [
    "Which pool rows are a drawn supplementary bout, shared by BOTH language",
    "implementations: drawnSupplementaryBout in internal/engine/competition.go",
    "(Go) and drawnSupplementaryBouts in web-mobile/js/admin_pools.jsx (JS, which",
    "reads the same rule from the wire fields). TestDrawnSupplementaryBout_SharedCases",
    "drives the Go side and the 'drawnSupplementaryBouts' block in",
    "web-mobile/js/__tests__/admin_pools.test.jsx the JS side. A change to the rule",
    "changes this table, and a copy that disagrees fails its own test.",
    "chusenCases is the second rule, the lots. ranked is the order a chusen",
    "recorded for rankedPool; inForce is the ids whose recorded rank still governs",
    "the bout's pool (poolRanksInForce in Go: a member of a group still level on",
    "points that no fought supplementary result settled; the JS reads it as the",
    "standings rows marked isOverridden). ruled is daihyosenRuledByChusen: the",
    "drawn representative bout's whole tied group (every team level on points",
    "with its two sides; standings lists the pool's rows as id and points, and a",
    "pool with no standings rules nothing) carries a rank in force. Two sides a",
    "correction no longer holds level are moot (a drawn tie-break bout too): settled, not ruled, owing no lots.",
    "So is a bout whose level group lies outside the band a tie is broken in: its standings rows carry tieOutOfBand (engine.tieNeedsBreak).",
    "stuck is what the Pools tab's notice names: drawn and not settled.",
    "ineligibleSides is the stamp a drawn tie-break bout carries on the wire (the Go side bars those ids in the competitor statuses): two barred sides settle it, nobody can fight it.",
    "An individual's lots follow a tie-break round the same way: a round that orders its whole group outlives them, and one that leaves the group level (a pair unfought, or a circle) keeps them in force."
  ],
